sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-10> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-10--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-10--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2025-wisdom-10: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.47" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.469"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.75"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Eye location after a specified channel misexpression is a standard, countable outcome, and the original paper reports percentages and body positions. Those embryo scores are not deposited, and public gene-expression resources for Pax6 do not contain the voltage experiment needed to compare competence. An outside reanalysis cannot confirm or refute the result without the raw series or a new experiment." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Misexpress potassium channels in Xenopus blastomeres outside the anterior neural field and score eye structures by location, including gut and tail, against lineage-tracer and Pax6-only controls. Eyes in posterior tissues after a voltage change, and not after the tracer alone, would support the claim; restriction of eyes to the anterior neural field would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Embryo-level locations and histological scores are published as summaries, not as a public table.", "There is no independent open replication dataset.", "Pax6 expression atlases do not record the voltage perturbation." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-10--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2025-wisdom-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.88" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.88"^^xsd:double ;
